nd more intense investment in  europe  the package encompasses research energy  production digital europe a european  energy union  it's about increasing europe's economic  potential in the medium term  that will also create more jobs  throughout europe  are you concerned that the variety of  projects will become a political  football that the 28 member countries  will be fighting to get the biggest  piece of  the allocations won't be made by the  european commission rather the european  investment bank  i consciously made this decision to keep  the project from becoming mired in  bureaucratic wrangling that often  produces bad choices  individual governments or parliaments  won't be able to put pressure on the  commission  the projects must be the kind that  wouldn't be undertaken without the  investment package  they must also be projects that present  a real potential for economic growth and  job creation  speaking of individual countries looking  at the ukraine crisis diplomatic efforts  are being made by individual nations  german chancellor merkel french  president hollande where is eu foreign  policy chief federica mogherini  knew full well why they did so and what  they were trying to accomplish  would it help if you played a bigger  role possibly as mediator  negotiating peace is much more important  as commission president is there  something you can offer russia that  might defuse the situation perhaps a  customs union  i'm sure you've noted that talks are  underway between germany france the eu  russia and ukraine  it makes no sense to comment on these  negotiations from the sidelines  we'll allow the negotiators to do their  job and keep our opinions to ourselves  you've changed sides so to speak for the  past 20 years you've held positions on  the european council and now you're eu  commissioned president do you feel you  have more power now that you can exert  more influences  questions like that leave me cold as  luxembourg prime minister and eurogroup  boss i did everything in my power to  manage the economic crisis  as commission president i can take  certain steps to promote economic growth  and job creation  i'm well acquainted with the member  nations and with the workings of the  commission  i have a broad view that keeps me on a  solid course  i did enjoy our interview
 

